    "field": "Global carbon cycle",
    "problem": "Existing global Gross Primary Production (GPP) products exhibit substantial performance variations and inaccuracies when validated, largely due to simplified model assumptions that fail to differentiate C3/C4 photosynthesis pathways or account for seasonal changes in photosynthetic capacity.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a method to generate a global gross primary production (GPP) dataset using an improved light use efficiency model that incorporates a state-of-the-art vegetation index gap-filling algorithm and a separate treatment for C3/C4 photosynthesis pathways, driven by satellite and climate data.",
    "task": "The task is to provide a new global moderate-resolution dataset of gross primary production (GPP) for vegetation from 2000\u20132016, using an improved light use efficiency model to overcome limitations in existing products.",
